; range_end_overflow: RANGE's exclusive bound is range-checked, not wrapped.
;
; start = 2^63 - 2, count = 3, so end = 2^63 + 1 is not representable. Rust
; computed it with `wrapping_add` and got 2^63 + 1 mod 2^64 = -(2^63 - 1),
; which is less than `current`, so the loop ran exactly one iteration;
; xqvm_py computed in unbounded integers and ran three. Different register
; contents, and different step counts -- and step count is metering on a
; chain that prices per step.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md ranges its overflow rule over every i64 operation the VM
; performs on a program's behalf. Loop control is not carved out of it.

PUSH 9223372036854775806   ; start
PUSH 3                     ; count
RANGE
LIDX r0
NEXT
HALT
